description=Knox Scanner writes the big moments of your run to a small text file, one line each: deaths, bites, bad injuries, towns, landmarks, the helicopter, the power grid, storms, hordes and milestones. <LINE> <LINE>
description=<H2> What to do with it <LINE> <TEXT>
description=A one-line command outside the game posts each line to a Discord channel. From there a bot, a stream overlay or your smart lights can react. The mod page has the commands. <LINE> <LINE>
description=<H2> Controls <LINE> <TEXT>
description=Options, Mods, Knox Scanner has a master switch and a tick box for every event. A short note above your character confirms each line. An optional key writes a request event. <LINE> <LINE>
description=<H2> Setup and limits <LINE> <TEXT>
description=No required mods. It runs on your own game and reports your own character. A multiplayer server must list KnoxScanner for its players to load it. The feed carries no player names. <LINE> <LINE>
description=The game cannot post by itself, so the outside command is needed. Safe to add or remove. No items, no saved data, nothing sent over the network. The first image is an illustration.
